{"name":"The Eightyone Glass","slug":"glyph-eightyone-glass","blurb":"On the trit street, Indra carries the glass toward the bracket lamp. The mark is Eightyone. Click the glass and it lights. A touch does not keep a step. A step away from the lamp is not kept. A step is kept only when the gap shrinks. The page proves its own street law on load. Glyph: The Eightyone Glass.","seal":"c2f22470abb36671be20475f200c89eebfb24b12f9a5f3129fb04cb836a03577"}
